{"connection_id": "BC-5e49f8f099e1b1aca9fa", "ref": "Mishnah Sanhedrin 5:1", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "seven witness inquiries", "note": "The commentary's suspicious report must be checked; the Mishnah specifies seven questions for examining capital witnesses, giving a concrete legal discipline for verification."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a1d8a31f68a5549e47c6", "ref": "Sirach 27:5", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speech as a test", "note": "The commentary glosses confirming a matter and also develops hearing; Sirach compares testing a person in conversation to testing pottery in a furnace. Speech becomes evidence of character."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9823d1e07bd32d5903b9", "ref": "Sirach 27:6", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "words reveal inner cultivation", "note": "The commentary says the mind works and the confirmed truth is conveyed; Sirach compares fruit revealing a tree's cultivation with words revealing the thought of a person's heart. It links outward speech to inward disposition."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a5fc10cb8046773bf224", "ref": "Sirach 27:6", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fruit reveals cultivation", "note": "The commentary joins inward mental work with outward truth; Sirach says fruit reveals a tree's cultivation just as speech reveals the thought of the heart. This makes observable expression evidence of inner character."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2cf8adcdc4b2d661a470", "ref": "Sirach 27:7", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hear before praising", "note": "The commentary connects hearing with verifying what is true; Sirach warns against praising someone before hearing them speak, since this is how people are tested. It gives listening an explicit evidentiary role."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cc45b22a4109f5890a59", "ref": "Sirach 2:2", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "steadfastness in calamity", "note": "The commentary ends with people urging one another to patience; Sirach tells the person serving God to set the heart right and be steadfast in a time of calamity. It makes patient endurance part of faithful service."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a928fac9736a1c5c1454", "ref": "Sirach 2:6", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "trust and hope in God", "note": "The commentary pairs belief with patience; Sirach tells the reader to trust God, hold fast, and hope in him. Its counsel binds trust to endurance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ad5a74e015ed03cede76", "ref": "Susanna (Theodotion) 51-59", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "separating and testing witnesses", "note": "The commentary cites checking a report before accepting it; Daniel separates the two elders and asks each where they saw Susanna, exposing their incompatible answers. This is a narrative of cross-examination overturning false testimony."}
