{"connection_id": "BC-cf7d01a85b08db46029c", "ref": "WLC:Isa.7.9", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "belief and firmness in one saying", "note": "The commentary defines iman as confirmation and haqq as becoming sure; Isaiah says that without believing, the hearers will not be established. The verse makes trust and firmness a deliberate Hebrew wordplay."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3b44f4b0f33c32b65761", "ref": "WLC:Isa.7.9", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "ء م ن / אמנ; table sound correspondence, unverified", "note": "The commentary's iman is confirmation; Isaiah repeats forms of the Hebrew אמנ root for believing and being established. The table's sound correspondence is unverified, while the Hebrew wordplay itself is explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-351f57eca3fdf2aad3c7", "ref": "WLC:Isa.7.9", "target": "sec8", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "ء م ن / אמנ; table sound correspondence", "note": "The commentary calls faith confirmed adherence to truth; Isaiah's warning plays on trusting and being established, making firmness the consequence of faith."}
