+{"connection_id":"BC-0a322aed61733174d0b0","ref":"WLC:Ps.17.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Being guarded as the pupil is protective imagery, not the eye's reflected small human image.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.17.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-70945d01141ceac6f7a2","ref":"WLC:Ps.19.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Divine command enlightening eyes is a metaphor for guidance, not a received report tested against observation.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.19.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3358ae6241dac3e02748","ref":"WLC:Ps.2.7","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalmist proclaims a divine decree, but neither checks it nor uses חקק as factual truth.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.2.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f5a84f63f7c7cde572df","ref":"WLC:Ps.27.13","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalmist believes he will see future goodness; John 20:29 and 1 Pet 1:8 already articulate belief without present sight.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.27.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-60de4461e00d5925ac27","ref":"WLC:Ps.27.13","status":"rejected","reason":"The אמנ form is genuine but this verse anticipates future sight rather than clarifying the root's trust-and-firmness range at Isa 7:9.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.27.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-270bd49cf529a8bf9545","ref":"WLC:Ps.27.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Faith before hoped-for sight duplicates the unseen-belief limit expressed by John 20:29 and 1 Pet 1:8.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.27.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-48874c05f7786023f988","ref":"WLC:Ps.27.13","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalmist's belief points toward later sight, a temporal pattern already contrasted with Thomas in the kept Gospel note.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.27.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bffc5ae852edccf132e9","ref":"WLC:Ps.34.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Taste and see the Lord's goodness is an invitation to experience, not investigation of whether another's news is true.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.34.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-55897ed63ecf205f3c5a","ref":"WLC:Ps.34.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Sensory tasting of divine goodness is metaphorical; the Queen's heard words checked by her eyes match ¶24-25's sequence more exactly.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.34.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bec97e24ccf0acb12588","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.3","status":"rejected","reason":"Trust and do good is a broad ethical pair; this section specifically argues a seeing, hearing and verification path.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0c75c8e8770720ee3455","ref":"WLC:Ps.48.9","status":"rejected","reason":"What was heard is now seen in God's city, a compact duplicate of the Queen's more explicit disbelief-until-sight account.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.48.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-99d6f62e28457c152c4a","ref":"WLC:Ps.73.16","status":"accepted","reason":"Trying to understand is called עמל, showing the root can denote difficult mental work.","paragraphs":[24],"evidence":["WLC:Eccl.2.11","WLC:Ps.73.16","WLC:Ps.73.17"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-671fd6c5b8adf1e02a26","ref":"WLC:Ps.73.17","status":"accepted","reason":"Entering God's sanctuary resolves the psalmist's toil over understanding, a specific movement from effort to insight.","paragraphs":[24],"evidence":["WLC:Eccl.2.11","WLC:Ps.73.16","WLC:Ps.73.17"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e9643c8813d36d59552b","ref":"WLC:Ps.78.32","status":"rejected","reason":"Israel's continued sin and unbelief in wonders shows signs need not persuade, already expressed by Isa 6's perception failure.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.78.32"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-10c3bcc9e18d029edb21","ref":"WLC:Ps.8.5","status":"accepted","reason":"Enosh denotes humanity remembered by God; the word does not state that humans are observers.","paragraphs":[24],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.8.5","WLC:Job.4.17","WLC:Ps.103.15","WLC:Dan.7.13"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-55deee095dbfe1b7c924","ref":"WLC:Ps.8.5","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse's enosh names mortal humanity under divine attention, a bounded cognate contrast to ¶24.","paragraphs":[24],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.8.5","WLC:Job.4.17","WLC:Ps.103.15","WLC:Dan.7.13"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e03f130cac470dec9655","ref":"WLC:Ps.89.2","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalmist proclaims God's faithfulness across generations; this is communal testimony but not a checked human report.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.89.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2d581e82f82956b0f2f4","ref":"WLC:Ps.89.2","status":"rejected","reason":"Emunah denotes divine fidelity announced orally, while ¶24's selected root note centers human trust and steadiness.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.89.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e6cdfd93c1abcdbc71d8","ref":"WLC:Ps.9.21","status":"rejected","reason":"Nations must learn they are enosh, but the human-mortality point is already stated by Ps 8:5 and Ps 103:15.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.9.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f51144ce25ed0717ec81","ref":"WLC:Ps.90.10","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalm names human years toil and trouble; Eccl 2:11 more directly ties עמל to work without gain.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.90.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2c6e08594fe1fbf44a9f","ref":"WLC:Ps.90.11","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC 90:11 concerns knowing divine wrath and contains no עמל; that word is in WLC 90:10.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.90.11","WLC:Ps.90.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4a010b486b2787b28a1a","ref":"WLC:Zech.8.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Speaking truth to a neighbour is an ethical rule; it does not say the statement has been tested against evidence as ¶25 proposes.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Zech.8.16"],"annotations":[]}

